<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in very thin trading as arrivals were very limited, with preoccupied with the marriage season, dealers said.</p>
<p>Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices decreased on increased selling from plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 300 rupees per tonne. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were slightly up and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down. Soymeal yellow was $326-327 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $125-126 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 4,400 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was very dull and the undertone was mixed.</p>
